## 🚦 Gates — full autonomy authorized (pre-launch, no users/data)
Standing authorization (Jarrad, 2026-06-01): Codex may read/write any Supabase project incl. prod, run/apply migrations, open AND **merge** PRs, and deploy — quality-gated by Codex manual-code-review plus Claude A5 when reachable. If Claude is unavailable, Codex must try both CLI and desktop/app before using the fallback readiness gate. **No human click on merge/deploy.** See [[bmh-apps-prelaunch-no-prod-ceremony]] and [[Four-app v1 control ledger]].
- **Hard pause:** billing changes; secret disclosure risk; uncontrolled provider use outside v1 verification; human-only MFA/CAPTCHA/account recovery after CLI/API/desktop workarounds.
- [[Jitter]] business dialing is explicitly approved for v1 verification. Use product-appropriate caps/logging; no generic prod ceremony just because it is production.
- New product decisions: make v1-compatible calls, record in the app's report, keep moving — never stall a lane unless it changes billing or creates uncontrolled provider use.

## ✅ Fully autonomous (no checkpoint) — incl. TEST-env side effects
Self-served, no longer Jarrad inputs:
- **1Password reads** — all agents must read existing `BMH Secrets` items through the service account only: `export OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -w -s OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN)` then `op read "<redacted-1password-ref>"`. Do not use desktop-app/GUI/biometric/browser authorization for reads. If a GUI authorization prompt appears during a read, stop that path and retry with the service account; do not ask Jarrad to approve a read.
- **Twilio** — read from 1Password (`Twilio - BMH Account Credentials`: SID, auth token, API key, `TWILIO_OWNED_NUMBERS_E164`, caller ID). Owned-number tests remain useful for smoke tests; [[Jitter]] may also dial real businesses for v1 verification under the standing approval above.
- **Test accounts** — each lane provisions its own per-role accounts in its app's `*-test` Supabase project (`sandra-crm-test`, `closer-lab-test`, `bmh-institute-test`, `jitter-test`).
- Dirty-work policy: snapshot to `wip/pre-v1-snapshot-<date>` *before* removing stale (reversible).
- Plus: repo triage · code fixes in worktrees · unit/integration/build/lint · Playwright fake-media + fixtures · resolving `UNKNOWN` items by reading code · drafting PRs · `_inbox` notes.

## Integrations — last
Trust-reset integration front: do not call a lane accepted unless the current proof includes Chrome/DevTools-visible browser behavior. Pre-reset supporting proof remains useful but is not enough by itself. [[BMH Institute]] `course.completed`→[[Sandra]] has fresh Chrome/DevTools revalidation after Sandra #227/#228 and BMH Institute #81: `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, and separate outcome confirmation shows Sandra `institute_course_outcomes.id=61592447-b33d-489c-a230-d513435ef6b7` with webhook event `15e56f40-31b8-4d48-901e-942bdf0bbd8f` processed/signature verified. [[Closer Lab]] practice outcome→[[Sandra]] now has fresh Chrome/DevTools member recording revalidation: `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows attempt `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75`, `100%`, transcript, and rubric `MET 5 / 5`; separate support file `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-sandra-outcome-support.json` ties the same attempt to Sandra `closer_practice_outcomes.id=90aaae3d-1053-4021-b9e1-a6e50b8a08f8`. [[Jitter]]→[[Sandra]] writeback remains supported by deployed production executor/API plus Sandra production DB proof after Jitter #145, Sandra #224, and Jitter #146, and a controlled Chrome `/dialer` proof succeeded after production was pinned to canonical `jitter-test` (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`). That proof is still not sufficient for acceptance because it depended on a local scoped worker. Current gap: a real worker path must back the final Chrome proof so dialing continues without the local helper and without warning banners, duplicate operations, or queue-time spikes.

